From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:50:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] BinaryAddonManager: lock the running add-ons when releasing
 one

GetAddonBase finds or adds an add-on under the lock, but ReleaseAddonBase
finds and erases it without one. An instance created on one thread while
another thread releases the last instance of the same add-on can race on
the map, or keep a base that is no longer listed, so the next instance
loads the add-on a second time.
---
 xbmc/addons/binary-addons/BinaryAddonManager.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/binary-addons/BinaryAddonManager.cpp b/xbmc/addons/binary-addons/BinaryAddonManager.cpp
--- a/xbmc/addons/binary-addons/BinaryAddonManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/addons/binary-addons/BinaryAddonManager.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,8 @@
 void CBinaryAddonManager::ReleaseAddonBase(const std::shared_ptr<CBinaryAddonBase>& addonBase,
                                            IAddonInstanceHandler* handler)
 {
+  std::unique_lock lock(m_critSection);
+
   const auto& addon = m_runningAddons.find(addonBase->ID());
   if (addon == m_runningAddons.end())
     return;
